okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: `muse --continue` freezes at launch with no response. Find and fix the cause."
symptom: "The launch window freezes right after start. Workspace log (9491, F:\\aap.ezonebot) stops after `remote_instructions_unchanged runtime=muse reason=launch` at 13:25:58 - no router spawn, no console-proxy lines, nothing."
investigation:
  isolation: "Isolated replay: `ciel_runtime.py muse --continue` from the repo tree, scratch workspace, isolated config dir (global config copy so the meta provider resolves), dedicated router port 9897, faulthandler stack dumps every 20s. Nothing touched the user's workspace state or their running Muse session."
  first_repro: "The launch died with `OSError: [WinError 995] The I/O operation has been aborted ...: '\\\\wsl.localhost\\Ubuntu-26.04\\home\\djlov\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions'` raised from channel_transcript_repository.latest() -> pathlib.glob -> os.stat, inside set_transcript_scope during the launch."
  environment: "Windows-side access to `\\\\wsl.localhost\\Ubuntu-26.04\\...` is wedged on this machine right now: a direct `ls` of that path hangs past 90s with no output, while the `wsl -e sh -lc` bridge answers the same directory in 0.19s. The user's freeze and this crash are the same call under the same condition (blocked stat vs aborted stat)."
  second_blocking_point: "With the launch unblocked, faulthandler dumps 20s apart showed the console-proxy poll loop ALSO stuck in the same latest()/glob/stat call - the poll loop consults transcripts every poll, so the TUI would freeze after start as well."
root_cause: "Transcript discovery globbed the transcript store synchronously on the caller's thread. For a WSL Muse the store is a UNC path (`\\\\wsl.localhost\\...`), so any stall or error of the WSL 9p relay is paid by the launch path and by the console-proxy poll loop. No deadline existed, and glob errors raised during lazy iteration escaped the try/except (which only wrapped the generator creation)."
fix:
  - "channel_transcript_repository.py: one shared daemon scan worker (_TranscriptScanWorker) runs every filesystem scan under TRANSCRIPT_SCAN_DEADLINE_SECONDS (2.5s). latest() serves the cached view when a scan is stuck or misses the deadline, and a missed deadline is retried no sooner than the TTL, so no caller thread ever blocks on the filesystem."
  - "Glob matches are materialized inside the guard, so OSError/WinError 995 raised during iteration is tolerated."
  - "The launch boundary scan (_capture_turn_scan_boundary) runs the whole scan+stat under the same deadline; a miss leaves the boundary unset and the delivery loop establishes it later."
verification:
  live_before: "Replay of the launch on the unfixed tree: crashed with WinError 995 (above); on the user's machine the same launch froze in the same call."
  live_after: "Same replay on the fixed tree under the still-wedged relay: the launch reaches `channel_windows_console_proxy_started` and the Muse TUI starts (argv observed inside WSL: `muse-bin-1.3.0-R3401.1 resume --yolo --model muse-spark-1.3 --reasoning-effort high --last`, confirming the --continue -> resume --last mapping end to end). Faulthandler dumps at 20/40/60s show the proxy main loop in its normal poll - no latest()/glob/stat frames."
  tests: "4 repository tests (glob iteration errors tolerated, wedged boundary returns at the deadline, cached view served while a scan is wedged, healthy boundary still pins the offset); unit 1570 OK (skipped=45), channel 410 OK (skipped=80); ruff clean; live router 9465 healthy before/after."
degradation: "While a relay stays wedged, transcript delta delivery lags (its background polls serve the cached view) and the turn boundary may be unset; both recover when the relay answers again. Tool delivery, input handling and the TUI itself are unaffected."
cleanup: "Two orphaned repro Muse TUIs sit in D state after their ConPTY owner was killed; they cannot be reclaimed until the relay/WSL unblocks. The user's own Muse session (pid 36399, R3233.1) was never touched. `~/.config/muse/settings.json` was changed by the isolated runs (the sync removed the router entry) and restored byte-identical from the pre-test backup."
environment_note: "The `\\\\wsl.localhost` relay to Ubuntu-26.04 is wedged machine-wide (also unrelated to Ciel Runtime). `wsl --shutdown` is the known remedy but would end the running Muse session and stop the Docker Desktop distros - user's decision."
